# Avalanche L1 two-data-center (2x2) benchmark configuration.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Everything is driven from a single CONTROL HOST: it runs the orchestration
# scripts, the load generator (bombard), and the Prometheus/Grafana monitoring
# stack. The control host never runs an L1 node itself.

# SSH user for every node (all nodes share one user).
SSH_USER=ubuntu

# Path on the control host to the SSH private key that reaches every node.
# All nodes must accept this key. Set it explicitly — if left unset a built-in
# default path is used, which is rarely what you want.
SSH_KEY_PATH=/home/ubuntu/.ssh/your-fleet-key

# =============================================================================
# TOPOLOGY — two data centers, BOTH ACTIVE (the 2x2 draft)
# =============================================================================
# One IP list per role, per data center. Each list's LENGTH sets that role's
# node count; its VALUES set placement. BOTH data centers run live, weighted L1
# validators — this is an active-active topology, not a primary/standby pair.
# The recommended 2x2 shape is 2 validators + 2 RPC trackers per DC:
#
#   validators  weighted L1 validators — consensus runs here (2 per DC).
#   RPC         pinned non-validating RPC trackers — the load-generator
#               ingress. Never promoted to validators.
#
# Node-to-DC mapping is explicit everywhere: DC A machines are named m1..mN,
# DC B machines b1..bN, and `reconcile endpoints` / status.sh print the site
# (a|b) for every node. Put DC B in a DIFFERENT region so the cross-DC latency
# is real (e.g. DC A in us-west-1, DC B in us-west-2).
#
# Any fleet box NOT listed here must have avalanchego STOPPED (pkill on the
# box) — a stray old process can keep a duplicate staking identity alive.
#
# CO-LOCATION: repeat an IP (within or across role lists / sites) to launch
# another avalanchego on that box; ports and data dirs auto-offset. Test-only —
# it trades away fault isolation.

# --- Data center A ------------------------------------------------------------
VALIDATOR_IPS=10.0.0.1,10.0.0.2   # 2 weighted validators in DC A
SPARE_IPS=                         # no hot spares in the 2x2 draft
RPC_IPS=10.0.0.5,10.0.0.6         # 2 RPC trackers in DC A (load-gen ingress)

# --- Data center B (required for 2x2; same shape as DC A) ----------------------
BACKUP_VALIDATOR_IPS=10.1.0.1,10.1.0.2   # 2 weighted validators in DC B
BACKUP_SPARE_IPS=
BACKUP_RPC_IPS=10.1.0.5,10.1.0.6         # 2 RPC trackers in DC B

# --- LEGACY positional format (still supported) ------------------------------
# If VALIDATOR_IPS is unset, the tooling falls back to a single positional list
# of exactly 6 IPs per site, in order: validators(3), spare(1), RPCs(2).
#   NODE_IPS=10.0.0.1,10.0.0.2,10.0.0.3,10.0.0.4,10.0.0.5,10.0.0.6
#   BACKUP_SITE_NODE_IPS=10.1.0.1,10.1.0.2,10.1.0.3,10.1.0.4,10.1.0.5,10.1.0.6
